{"code":200,"text":"OK","success":true,"data":{"id":755587,"excludedCurrencies":null,"title":"Crypto Transactions Policy","content":"<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>1. INTRODUCTION<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top:16px\">This Crypto Policy establishes the framework for BETSSEN. (&quot;the Company&quot;) to manage risks associated with the use of cryptocurrencies on its gaming platform. It aligns with Cura&ccedil;ao Gaming Authority (CGA) regulatory requirements, Anti-Money Laundering (AML), Counter-Financing of Terrorism (CFT) obligations, and Responsible Gaming principles.<\/p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>2. PURPOSE AND OBJECTIVES<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Ensure compliance with applicable laws and regulations concerning cryptocurrencies.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Prevent misuse of the platform for illicit activities including money laundering, terrorism financing, and fraud.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Safeguard user assets and maintain system integrity in handling digital currencies.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Promote transparency, integrity, and operational accountability.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Mitigate operational, market, and cybersecurity risks.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>3. SCOPE<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<p>This policy applies to:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">All BETSSEN, departments, employees, and contractors.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Third-party service providers involved in crypto transactions.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Users engaging in gaming activities using cryptocurrencies.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>4. GOVERNANCE STRUCTURE<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Compliance Officer (CO) and Money Laundering Reporting Officer (MLRO) oversee policy implementation.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">A Crypto Risk Committee (CRC) may be convened to assess crypto-specific risks and report to senior management.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Key roles include wallet management, transaction monitoring, and regulatory reporting.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>5. APPROVED CRYPTOCURRENCIES<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<p>Supported tokens:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Bitcoin (BTC)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Binance Coin (BNB)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">TRON (TRX)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Dogecoin (DOGE)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Solana (SOL)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Shiba Inu (SHIB)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Ethereum (ETH)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Ripple (XRP)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Litecoin (LTC)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">USDT (ERC-20)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">USDT (TRC-20)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Bitcoin Cash (BCH)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Cardano (ADA)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Stellar (XLM)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Dai (DAI)<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Additional tokens subject to risk and compliance review.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>Each token undergoes due diligence for liquidity, volatility, anonymity, and reputation.<\/p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>6. WALLET INFRASTRUCTURE AND KEY MANAGEMENT<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Hot Wallets: Daily transactions; protected with multi-signature (Multisig).<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Cold Wallets: Long-term storage; offline and hardware-encrypted.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Key Management: Encrypted private keys stored in HSMs; 2 senior managers required for cold storage transfers.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Disaster Recovery Plan: Includes key recovery and continuity measures.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>7. USER ONBOARDING AND KYC REQUIREMENTS<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Verification includes:\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li style=\"list-style-type:circle\">Government-issued ID<\/li>\n\t\t<li style=\"list-style-type:circle\">Proof of address<\/li>\n\t\t<li style=\"list-style-type:circle\">Selfie with document (liveness check with&nbsp; 3rd party KYC tool)<\/li>\n\t\t<li style=\"list-style-type:circle\">Sanctions and PEP screening<\/li>\n\t<\/ul>\n\t<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) for high-risk users and jurisdictions.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>8. CRYPTO TRANSACTION MONITORING<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Incoming wallet addresses screened with blockchain analytics tools (e.g., Chainalysis).<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Block deposits linked to darknet, mixers, or sanctioned entities.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Risk triggers include high volume\/frequency and privacy-enhancing tokens.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>9. AML\/CFT TRANSACTION CONTROLS<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Automated and manual monitoring of transactions.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Flag structuring, layering, anonymous wallets, and rapid deposit-withdrawal patterns.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">MLRO to file reports to Financial Intelligence Unit (FIU) as required.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>10. CRYPTO WITHDRAWALS<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Only pre-approved wallets verified during KYC.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Manual review for withdrawals over EUR 1000 or changes to withdrawal addresses.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>11. TRANSACTION LIMITS<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<p>To ensure operational security and compliance with regulatory requirements, the following transaction limits are applied:<\/p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\">Per Transaction Limits<\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Deposit: Minimum $10, Maximum $10,000 equivalent in cryptocurrency.<br \/>\n\t&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Withdrawal: Minimum $10, Maximum $3,000 equivalent.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\">Daily Cumulative Limit<\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Maximum withdrawal per user per day: $7,000 USD\/EUR equivalent.<br \/>\n\t&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Once reached, users must wait 24 hours before additional withdrawals.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\">Weekly Cumulative Limit<\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Maximum withdrawal per user per week: $15,000 USD\/EUR equivalent.<br \/>\n\t&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Once reached, users must wait 7 days from the last completed withdrawal.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\">Exceptions and Approvals<\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Adjusted limits for VIP users or exceptional cases require approval from the MLRO and senior management.<br \/>\n\t&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Enhanced KYC and AML checks are mandatory for such exceptions.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\">Real-Time Monitoring<\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Alerts are triggered for threshold breaches, and transactions may be temporarily frozen pending manual review.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>12. ACCOUNTING, RECONCILIATION, AND REPORTING<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Daily reconciliation of crypto balances with user ledgers.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Variance reporting and audit trails maintained.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Annual external audits of crypto systems.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>13. DATA RETENTION AND SECURITY<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Retain crypto transaction and KYC data for at least 5 years.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Encrypt all data in compliance with GDPR and applicable laws.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Semi-annual penetration testing and security audits.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>14. THIRD-PARTY SERVICE PROVIDERS<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Vet exchanges, custodians, and payment processors for AML\/CFT controls, licensing, and security.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Regular compliance reviews and Service Level Agreements (SLAs).<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>15. STAFF TRAINING AND AWARENESS<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Annual crypto-specific AML\/CFT training.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Scenario-based training for red flags.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Awareness programs on phishing and social engineering.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>16. POLICY ENFORCEMENT<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Violations may result in disciplinary actions, contract termination, and reporting to authorities.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\"><strong>17. POLICY REVIEW AND MAINTENANCE<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"list-style-type:disc\">Reviewed annually and updated for regulatory or technological changes.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:19px\">&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/h3>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n","metaDescription":null,"metaTitle":null,"metaUrl":null}}